{
  "_doc": "How each monster comes to know where the hero is (src/senses.py; Brandon, 2026-11-12: no monster knows where you are unless it is thematically and lore appropriate). Every monster sees (a real line of sight, within its perception_range, default 8) and hears (the noise the hero makes). Some have a lore sense on top, listed under 'families' (every member) and 'monsters' (one kind; it replaces the family's list). 'blind' takes sight away. Ranges are tiles. A sense that goes 'through_walls' finds the hero behind stone; 'needs_motion' fails while he stands still; 'sees_invisible' is not fooled by invisibility. 'line' is said the first time on a floor that a kind finds him that way, when it is within 'line_reach' tiles; it teaches the sense.",
  "line_reach": 12,
  "senses": {
    "scent": {
      "range": 8,
      "through_walls": true,
      "sees_invisible": true,
      "line": "{The} lifts its head and sniffs the air. It has your scent."
