  "noise": {
    "_doc": "Radii in tiles, measured along open ground (sound goes round corners and through doorways, not through stone; a closed door muffles it by 'door_cost' tiles). Footsteps: 'step' at DEX 10, one tile quieter for every 'dex_per_tile' points of DEX over 10 (never below 1), 'burdened' louder with a heavy pack; Cat's Footfall and silent walking make none. A monster already hunting the hero listens harder: 'hunter_bonus'.",
    "step": 3,
    "dex_per_tile": 4,
    "burdened": 2,
    "hunter_bonus": 3,
    "door_cost": 3,
    "melee": 8,
    "shot": 5,
    "spell": 6,
    "door": 5,
    "coin": 4,
    "struck": 8,
    "alarm": 12,
    "squeak": 60
  },
  "waking": {
    "_doc": "A creature asleep (not a deep sleeper of a zoo, graveyard or barracks: those have their own odds in src/sleepers.py) may wake when it hears something. 'step_near' is the chance per step heard within 'near' tiles, 'step_far' beyond that; 'loud' is for fights, doors, alarms and coin, 'loud_far' beyond half the noise's reach. The hero's DEX, Cat's Footfall, silent walking, the Hand of Glory and a heavy pack change the footstep odds as they do for the deep sleepers.",
    "near": 2,
    "step_near": 0.25,
    "step_far": 0.06,
    "loud": 0.7,
    "loud_far": 0.3,
    "deep_loud_reach": 3,
    "deep_loud": 0.2
  },
  "search": {
    "_doc": "A creature that loses the hero goes to the last place it saw, smelled or heard him and searches there for a while ('turns', more if it was roused by an alarm or a call for help), then gives up and goes back to what it was doing. 'lost_line' is said when one the hero can see gives up.",
    "turns": [
      6,
      12
    ],
    "roused_turns": [
      14,
      22
    ],
    "radius": 4,
    "lost_line": "{The} loses your trail and turns away."
  },
  "jobs": {
    "_doc": "What a creature does before it notices the hero, chosen when the floor is made (populate_floor): 'wander' roams from room to room, 'guard' keeps its post and turns to look, 'sleep' sleeps until something wakes it. Weights by family; a pack shares one job. Ambushers, mimics, rooted things, named foes and the bosses keep their own ways.",
